WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Two more pieces.

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.950
First, the extract doesn't send anything.

3
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.961
It writes a file in the
HR middleware's layout,

4
00:00:06.961 --> 00:00:11.600
and the middleware from Book 19's
Chapter 01 builds the skim requests.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.600
Its dry run is its default, so nothing
reaches a tenant unless you ask it to.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.806
And in Module 1's register, inbound
provisioning already names both

7
00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:25.162
the HR app and the contractor-source
app, through that same middleware.

8
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:27.125
Second, the sponsor review.

9
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:30.750
It goes on the contractor access
package's assignment policy.

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.200
It runs twice a year.

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.088
The manager, who is the sponsor,
reviews, with a named fallback reviewer.

12
00:00:37.088 --> 00:00:40.350
And when nobody responds,
access is removed.

13
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.926
One caution from the kit: using the
requestor's manager as a reviewer

14
00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:49.080
is among the things it lists as
unconfirmed, so Lab 2 checks it.
